# Personal, machine-scoped Claude config — never commit (course L2: "local" scope)
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/CLAUDE.local.md

# Quetrex runtime artifacts.
# Whitelist form on purpose: everything the gates write at runtime is ignored,
# and only the two PROJECT CONFIG artifacts are tracked. A new runtime artifact
# is therefore ignored by default instead of leaking into a commit.
#   tracked : project.json (kanban binding), verify.json (the verify chain)
#   ignored : verify-ledger.jsonl, verify-attempts, ESCALATION, state.json,
#             review-verdict.json, security-findings.json, qa-report.json,
#             plan/, build/
# git-workflow must stage explicit paths — never `git add -A` — because a
# commit that sweeps these in moves HEAD out from under a sha-pinned verdict.
.quetrex/*
!.quetrex/project.json
!.quetrex/verify.json
